Fuel additives are specialized chemical formulations incorporated into fuels to improve performance, stability, combustion efficiency, and compatibility with engines and industrial equipment. They help control sludge formation, reduce deposits, protect components against corrosion, and improve fuel handling under different operating conditions.

The market serves marine transportation, power generation, industrial boilers, and other fuel-consuming sectors. Demand is influenced by fuel quality standards, environmental regulations, operational efficiency targets, and the need to maintain equipment reliability. Manufacturers are increasingly developing multifunctional formulations designed to address several performance requirements while helping customers comply with changing environmental standards.

